"# Conversation history of an agent\n\nUse aos-agent history to list, delete, summarize or replace messages in one agent's conversation.\n\n```sh\naos-agent history -t NAME ls            # one message per line: LINE, ROLE, TEXT\naos-agent history -t NAME ls -j 5-      # lines 5 to the end, as JSON\naos-agent history -t NAME rm 3-4\naos-agent history -t NAME summarize 1-6 \"User said their favorite color is blue.\"\naos-agent history -t NAME set 2 '{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"...\"}'\n```\n\n`summarize` writes one message that reads `aos: summary (lines A-B, N messages): TEXT` (role `user` unless `--role`); `set` writes the message as given.\n\nNo action means `ls`. A range is `N`, `A-B` or `A-`. `--target NAME` defaults to `$AOS_AGENT`.\n\nRemoved or replaced messages are kept in `history_removed.jsonl` next to the history. `--keep FILE` puts them elsewhere; `--no-keep` drops them (asks first; `-y` skips the question).\n\nPause a running agent first: `aos-agent ctl pause NAME`. A running fsm agent uses the change from its next request. An eca agent (claude, codex) starts a new conversation on its next turn and carries the changed record over.\n\nErrors: `TargetMissing`, `HistoryMissing`, `RangeBad` (bad range, or a line of the step in progress).\n\nAn agent changes its own history with tool `self_history`: see `me.json#/self_history`.\n"
